WEBVTT

00:10.650 --> 00:14.010
<i>Right now Usagi-san is stressed to the max.</i>

00:17.950 --> 00:22.360
<i>That's definitely because, not only did he show up to the party, which he hates the most,</i>

00:22.550 --> 00:26.450
<i>but on top of that he ran into his elder brother, whom he hates even more.</i>

00:27.280 --> 00:31.430
<i>Plus, for some reason, his brother sent me flowers...</i>

00:33.110 --> 00:35.540
<i>I have to be very careful not to provoke him in anyway...</i>

00:36.360 --> 00:40.400
<i>because everything always ends up falling on me.</i>

00:43.190 --> 00:44.620
Hey, Usagi-san,

00:45.010 --> 00:47.490
drinking or smoking- pick one.

00:49.990 --> 00:53.360
This party's just another part of your work, right?

00:54.070 --> 00:55.640
I never asked for one.

00:56.000 --> 00:58.930
Hey, I don't think that's a very nice thing to say.

00:59.080 --> 01:01.860
It doesn't hurt to get a taste of lowly human society once in a while.

01:04.560 --> 01:08.770
If I had to get a taste of anything, I'd rather get a taste of your...

01:10.420 --> 01:12.890
I did you a favor and came all the way here with you,

01:12.890 --> 01:14.770
so just go and smile for the crowd already!

01:15.200 --> 01:16.280
Thanks for the food.

01:17.660 --> 01:21.030
What? I'm here only because you said you wanted to come.

01:21.830 --> 01:23.090
Huh? What?

01:24.110 --> 01:24.740
Nothing.

01:25.860 --> 01:26.920
Geez.

01:27.730 --> 01:29.640
I am not that free too you know.

01:30.160 --> 01:33.200
I need to study for the second semester finals.

01:35.790 --> 01:37.000
Sometimes it's okay, right?

01:38.190 --> 01:41.300
Staying in a suite together enjoying that lovey-dovey couple feeling.

01:42.340 --> 01:44.740
Who and who are lovey-dovey?

01:45.450 --> 01:48.240
Why do you insist on not admitting it?

01:48.700 --> 01:49.700
Admitting what?

01:50.970 --> 01:54.840
Till this day, you've never once told me you love me.

01:54.990 --> 01:58.140
E-Eh? W-Why bring this up suddenly?

01:58.210 --> 02:02.110
I-I've said it before. I just don't remember when.

02:02.570 --> 02:07.910
You're "I love you" is always preceded by an "I think" or followed by "probably".

02:09.490 --> 02:10.590
What's wrong with that?

02:10.970 --> 02:14.620
We're both Japanese, let's play it a little vague.

02:18.150 --> 02:20.330
How about accepting it already.

02:21.340 --> 02:23.560
Accept... what?

02:24.130 --> 02:26.300
"I love you, Usagi-san."

02:26.400 --> 02:27.050
What?

02:27.220 --> 02:30.580
'Whenever I think about Usagi-san, my head feels funny..."

02:30.580 --> 02:31.450
No way!

02:31.630 --> 02:33.230
"...my whole body feels like it's burning..."

02:33.270 --> 02:34.700
No way, no way!

02:34.700 --> 02:37.220
"...I can't even live without you..."

02:37.220 --> 02:39.770
No way!!

02:40.300 --> 02:44.610
By the way, stop taking out your stress on me!

02:51.890 --> 02:53.480
Cut it out!

02:53.710 --> 02:57.120
Do you think you can do anything to someone as long as you're in love with them!?

02:59.010 --> 03:00.110
I do.

03:02.110 --> 03:03.750
Oh, do you now...

03:04.130 --> 03:05.680
Is there a problem with that?

03:07.080 --> 03:07.800
No.

03:07.960 --> 03:12.900
What happens twice can happen thrice

03:12.990 --> 03:18.240
Afuredashita shoudou ga bokura no mune wo ustu

03:12.990 --> 03:18.240
An overflowing urge moves our hearts

03:16.940 --> 03:30.210
Junjou Romantica 2

03:18.240 --> 03:21.710
ima futari no story

03:18.240 --> 03:21.710
Now, our story...

03:23.000 --> 03:30.490
bokura no mirai ga kagayaite yuku yo

03:23.000 --> 03:30.490
Our future is going to shine on.

03:33.930 --> 03:39.220
mae ni susumeba dareka to butsukatte

03:33.930 --> 03:39.220
If I try to move forward, I collide with someone else,

03:39.690 --> 03:44.050
okubyou ni naru bakari

03:39.690 --> 03:44.050
and always lose my nerve.

03:44.050 --> 03:49.650
dakedo mae wo muite aruite iku yo

03:44.050 --> 03:49.650
But I'm going to face front and walk ahead,

03:49.650 --> 03:53.280
kimi to aeru nara

03:49.650 --> 03:53.280
if it means I can see you.

03:55.310 --> 04:00.290
ame ni utarete furueru koe

03:55.310 --> 04:00.290
Your trembling voice, pelted by the rain,

04:00.620 --> 04:05.890
nemurenu yoru wo samayottemo

04:00.620 --> 04:05.890
even if I have to wander sleepless nights,

04:06.570 --> 04:09.370
boku wa yuku yo

04:06.570 --> 04:09.370
I'll go,

04:09.370 --> 04:16.120
kimi to deaeru sono hima de

04:09.370 --> 04:16.120
Until the day when I can see you.

04:16.940 --> 04:22.130
Afuredashita shoudou ga bokura no mune wo ustu

04:16.940 --> 04:22.130
An overflowing urge moves our hearts

04:22.130 --> 04:25.840
ima futari no story

04:22.130 --> 04:25.840
Now, our story

04:26.000 --> 04:27.650
ugokidashita

04:26.000 --> 04:27.650
has started.

04:27.650 --> 04:32.640
meguriatta shougeki de iro no nai sekai ga

04:27.650 --> 04:32.640
The impact of our meeting, shocked this dull, grey world

04:32.640 --> 04:39.830
isshun de azayaka ni irozuite yuku yo

04:32.640 --> 04:39.830
and instantly burst into a brilliant color.

04:43.830 --> 04:49.240
I'll start by explaining the basic procedure for the ceremony and the layout of the hall.

04:49.480 --> 04:52.450
Though it should be fairly straight forward, I think.

04:52.990 --> 04:54.200
Isaka-san, you're basically...

04:54.200 --> 04:55.150
What's wrong?

04:55.250 --> 05:00.040
Oh, no,... I just can't seem to get my tie straight.

05:01.220 --> 05:02.130
Let me see.

05:05.040 --> 05:07.440
I sort of look like a kid.

05:07.980 --> 05:08.910
You are a kid.

05:10.180 --> 05:14.770
But I can't help it. It's only my third time wearing a suit.

05:16.060 --> 05:16.780
Alright!

05:16.780 --> 05:19.120
Sensei! Please come here!

05:20.290 --> 05:22.540
Sensei, you're going to stand by, let's see...

05:23.600 --> 05:25.040
...by those flowers.

05:25.540 --> 05:27.310
Hey, are you listening?

05:27.780 --> 05:28.600
Cutie.

05:29.490 --> 05:32.160
I wanted to talk to you about something. Is it okay?

05:34.260 --> 05:36.970
I've been wanting to tell this to you for quiet some time.

05:37.260 --> 05:38.480
This is a good opportunity.

05:40.200 --> 05:43.480
I don't want you to get close to Akihiko than is necessary.

05:45.660 --> 05:47.580
What are you saying suddenly?

05:48.210 --> 05:51.800
Akihiko and I have known each other since we were kids.

05:51.990 --> 05:54.940
So I know his personality like the back of my hand.

05:55.060 --> 05:59.020
U-Um, aren't you misunderstanding something?

05:59.340 --> 06:02.010
Usagi-san and I aren't...

06:02.840 --> 06:05.470
He's attractive and talented, right?

06:05.640 --> 06:08.160
People around him just can't leave him alone...

06:08.320 --> 06:11.100
...in a good way and a bad way.

06:12.220 --> 06:18.980
I don't want Akihiko to get caught up in anything unnecessary or scandalous.

06:19.840 --> 06:23.770
Since you're a smart kid, you understand what I'm getting at, right?

06:25.350 --> 06:27.150
Um, Isaka-san.

06:27.470 --> 06:29.900
I think you're misunderstanding something.

06:31.360 --> 06:35.600
I'm just...just, crashing at his place for now, that's all.

06:35.870 --> 06:39.360
Usagi-san is my brother's friend, he's just my landlord.

06:39.730 --> 06:40.660
Is that so?

06:40.730 --> 06:41.820
Of course!

06:42.000 --> 06:45.010
Usagi-san and I have nothing to do with each other!

06:46.320 --> 06:48.040
<i>No, that didn't sound right...</i>

06:50.770 --> 06:54.260
I sell products for a living, for making money.

06:54.540 --> 06:57.990
So I think of what I can do to increase those sales.

06:58.780 --> 07:03.260
For that, I cut off anything unnecessary that's getting in my way.

07:04.100 --> 07:04.760
Sorry.

07:04.960 --> 07:10.300
Well, if there's nothing between you guys, then I guess I'm worrying over nothing.

07:10.450 --> 07:11.690
Forget about it.

07:12.270 --> 07:16.260
Anyway, the party will be starting soon. Take a good look around.

07:17.920 --> 07:21.270
Stay too close to someone and you end up not being able to see them at all.

07:22.230 --> 07:24.990
You too don't want to cause trouble for anyone, right?

07:26.710 --> 07:27.880
<i>Trouble...?</i>

07:32.600 --> 07:39.830
So then, without further ado, welcome to Usami Akihiko-sensei's Kikukawa Award celebration party!

07:37.530 --> 07:40.520
Usami Akihiko/ Kikukawa Award Celebration/ Hosted by Marukawa Publishing

07:42.150 --> 07:48.760
<i>What Isaka-san was trying to say is, to make sure nobody finds out that Usagi-san is going out with me, a guy.</i>

07:49.890 --> 07:51.540
<i>Meaning, don't get close to him, right?</i>

07:52.290 --> 07:54.590
<i>Well, it's not like I'm going out with him.</i>

07:55.830 --> 08:00.400
<i>In any case, it was Usagi-san who hit on me in the first place.</i>

08:01.400 --> 08:03.440
<i>How much does Isaka-san know?</i>

08:04.130 --> 08:07.830
<i>I can never understand what that guy is thinking.</i>

08:08.790 --> 08:10.340
<i>I mean, I did the safe thing by denying it,</i>

08:11.130 --> 08:12.700
<i>but, just that...</i>

08:13.360 --> 08:18.660
<i>I feel kind of, a little, just a tiny bit mad at myself for that...</i>

08:19.650 --> 08:23.340
Ladies and gentlemen, a few words from Usami-sensei on winning the award.

08:28.350 --> 08:29.870
I'm Usami Akihiko.

08:30.120 --> 08:31.540
<i>Who are you!?</i>

08:33.490 --> 08:36.990
I would like to thank everyone for making the time from your busy schedules to come all this way,

08:37.390 --> 08:43.330
and am incredibly grateful for this amazing celebration that you've all made possible.

08:38.050 --> 08:40.350
Ahh, Aikawa-san!

08:40.350 --> 08:42.900
This is fraud! Everyone's been tricked!

08:43.830 --> 08:46.530
Misaki-kun, this is what it means to be an adult.

08:48.050 --> 08:55.070
This novel, for which I was honored to receive the Kikukawa Award, is somewhat unique compared to my other books.

08:53.810 --> 08:55.440
<i>Oh, my my!</i>

08:56.000 --> 08:59.230
<i>Phony smile plastered on his face, putting on the nice guy act.</i>

08:59.570 --> 09:02.520
<i>Everyone, don't be fooled!</i>

09:02.600 --> 09:05.190
<i>His personality is totally crazy.</i>

09:06.270 --> 09:09.800
<i>He can't do anything other that write novels!</i>

09:10.400 --> 09:12.520
<i>He's a giant, raging pervert!</i>

09:16.130 --> 09:17.590
Thank you very much!

09:20.300 --> 09:22.080
<i>What's up with that cool face?</i>

09:22.620 --> 09:23.900
<i>I'll bring him down a notch!</i>

09:24.160 --> 09:25.090
Usagi-san!

09:28.300 --> 09:30.800
Usami-sensei, congratulations!

09:31.040 --> 09:32.640
Congratulations!

09:32.720 --> 09:37.840
I read your book and was really moved by it!

09:38.030 --> 09:39.230
Thank you very much.

09:39.380 --> 09:40.930
Please enjoy yourselves.

09:42.120 --> 09:43.060
Usagi-san!

09:43.660 --> 09:44.650
Usami-sensei!

09:44.820 --> 09:46.340
Congratulations!

09:55.020 --> 09:55.910
Misaki...

09:56.090 --> 09:57.450
Here here, Usami-sensei!

10:00.560 --> 10:02.170
This is Sumi-sensei.

10:02.170 --> 10:04.940
He was a selection committee member this time.

10:05.290 --> 10:06.610
Congratulations!

10:06.780 --> 10:09.920
I always look forward to your work.

10:09.920 --> 10:10.800
Thank you very much.

10:10.800 --> 10:13.340
<i>Usagi-san... might be really amazing.</i>

10:10.800 --> 10:14.090
I too enjoy your books very much.

10:14.340 --> 10:17.900
<i>I mean, I know that he's a popular author and all that, but...</i>

10:19.020 --> 10:21.970
Oh! Isn't that the actress Tsukishiro Aya?

10:21.970 --> 10:23.200
It's really her!

10:23.200 --> 10:24.970
Why is she here?

10:25.020 --> 10:28.140
Because they are turning the novel into a movie, right?

10:28.140 --> 10:29.240
She's playing the heroine.

10:29.750 --> 10:31.090
No way! Really!?

10:34.100 --> 10:36.050
Will Usami-san be okay?

10:36.170 --> 10:38.400
That women's known to be a man-eater!

10:39.400 --> 10:41.070
Don't say things like that!

10:40.240 --> 10:45.810
Even with an actress standing next to him, he still looks every bit charming. Amazing, isn't he?

10:47.450 --> 10:53.080
I don't want Akihiko to get caught up in anything unnecessary or scandalous.

10:54.080 --> 10:55.480
<i>Generally speaking...</i>

10:56.540 --> 10:57.970
<i>...two men staying together...</i>

10:58.160 --> 11:00.270
<i>...is risky... right?</i>

11:00.690 --> 11:02.180
Trouble

11:02.940 --> 11:05.460
<i>Will I be causing Usagi-san any trouble...?</i>

11:06.490 --> 11:08.670
<i>For me, that word is the most...</i>

11:12.320 --> 11:13.050
Please.

11:13.050 --> 11:16.930
Eh... Ah... T-Thank you.

11:17.390 --> 11:21.710
I must apologize for that unsightly scene you had to witness the other day.

11:22.720 --> 11:27.600
Let me introduce myself again. I'm Isaka-san's secretary, Asahina.

11:28.990 --> 11:30.630
Oh, nice to meet you.

11:31.040 --> 11:33.030
Is it your first time at such an event?

11:33.410 --> 11:34.520
A-Ah, yes.

11:34.870 --> 11:38.750
I've been to a few but it's no good.

11:38.990 --> 11:41.870
I'm never quiet comfortable with these glitzy parties.

11:42.800 --> 11:46.380
<i>Is he perhaps trying to be considerate of me?</i>

11:46.680 --> 11:49.370
Since this is a good chance, would you like to have something to eat?

11:49.850 --> 11:54.370
Um, thank you very much. But I need to go to the bathroom.

11:57.970 --> 12:01.520
<i>I think I understand now, what Isaka-san was trying to say.</i>

12:05.030 --> 12:08.000
<i>Even if Usagi-san himself says its okay, still...</i>

12:09.030 --> 12:13.250
<i>...as long as I'm here, it'll be trouble for him in the end.</i>

12:17.040 --> 12:18.180
<i>That's no good.</i>

12:18.670 --> 12:21.760
<i>I don't want to ever cause trouble for anyone.</i>

12:23.490 --> 12:25.580
<i>Especially not for Usagi-san...</i>

12:27.530 --> 12:29.030
Excu-

12:32.240 --> 12:33.540
<i>Usagi the elder...</i>

12:40.640 --> 12:43.400
D-Did you stay here?

12:44.850 --> 12:47.520
I made a reservation here thinking I might be able to meet you.

12:48.100 --> 12:50.100
But never really thought I'd actually meet you...

12:52.220 --> 12:54.080
I have many things to talk about.

12:54.640 --> 12:55.690
Please follow me.

12:56.070 --> 12:58.240
Eh? Um... I...

12:59.420 --> 13:00.430
Come in.

13:05.060 --> 13:07.840
T-T-T-Thank you for the food.

13:08.860 --> 13:09.760
<i>This is bad.</i>

13:09.840 --> 13:14.370
<i>Yesterday, I really went and gave this gentleman here a piece of my mind...</i>

13:15.750 --> 13:17.050
Moron!!!

13:19.110 --> 13:22.630
<i>He was blaming Usagi-san for all this crap, so I acted a little rude myself.</i>

13:23.530 --> 13:25.690
<i>It was his fault in the first place,</i>

13:26.190 --> 13:29.130
<i>so I don't think there's anything for me to apologize for, but...</i>

13:29.960 --> 13:34.620
<i>But that "moron!!!" had about an year's supply of "moron" in it...</i>

13:32.810 --> 13:37.920
A normal "moron".
An year's supply of
"morooooooon!"

13:36.070 --> 13:37.760
<i>What to do, what to do!</i>

13:39.530 --> 13:43.330
Um... Thank you very much for the flowers!

13:45.060 --> 13:47.310
But... why the flowers?

13:48.760 --> 13:50.270
You like flowers, right?

13:50.640 --> 13:52.380
You said so before, at least.

13:54.170 --> 13:58.550
O-Oh, that. Well, I just said that because I happened to have some flowers with me...

13:59.200 --> 14:01.560
But it's not like I dislike them or anything.

14:03.250 --> 14:05.490
Then what do you like?

14:07.120 --> 14:10.750
Especially, um... let's see...

14:11.570 --> 14:14.930
...That's right... Strawberries...

14:22.930 --> 14:23.910
What's this?

14:24.670 --> 14:25.580
It's a strawberry.

14:26.370 --> 14:27.620
It's a strawberry alright.

14:28.710 --> 14:30.580
You said you like strawberries.

14:31.400 --> 14:33.070
Ah? ...yes.

14:36.990 --> 14:38.320
<i>What should I do, Nii-chan!?</i>

14:38.540 --> 14:40.380
<i>I can't match his tempo!</i>

14:40.630 --> 14:43.440
<i>What am I supposed to do when talking to people like this again...!?</i>

14:43.730 --> 14:45.820
<i>Help!</i>

14:46.860 --> 14:49.390
Has it been long since you moved in with Akihiko?

14:49.840 --> 14:52.910
Oh, no. Just from this past April.

14:53.550 --> 14:56.250
It must be a pain living with him, right?

14:57.020 --> 15:00.090
I'm sure, he doesn't even know how to clean up after himself.

15:00.600 --> 15:03.040
Speaking of which, I do all the chores.

15:03.170 --> 15:04.640
That's how I pay my rent.

15:04.830 --> 15:06.400
You do all the housework?

15:06.990 --> 15:07.680
Yes.

15:09.050 --> 15:10.030
I see.

15:11.230 --> 15:12.940
And even though you are so young. I'm impressed.

15:13.770 --> 15:17.020
Well, you're still young yourself, Haruhiko-san.

15:17.120 --> 15:19.010
Um, how old are you...?

15:19.450 --> 15:20.880
Two years older than he is.

15:21.290 --> 15:25.840
Oh! But I couldn't tell at all until it was pointed out.

15:26.090 --> 15:28.120
You and Usagi-san don't look alike that much.

15:29.310 --> 15:29.760
<i>Huh?</i>

15:31.300 --> 15:33.510
It's natural that we don't look alike.

15:34.160 --> 15:40.680
<i>Oh... I don't quiet understand, but I definitely said something that irritated him.</i>

15:42.040 --> 15:44.820
U-Um, I should be going back.

15:45.120 --> 15:46.270
Thank you for the cake.

15:47.730 --> 15:50.300
The party will still be going on for a while, so it's okay, isn't it?

15:50.710 --> 15:52.360
Stay here for a bit.

15:52.840 --> 15:55.160
O-Oh no, I'm sorry.

15:55.320 --> 15:59.420
I had just slipped out for a moment. I should go back to Usagi-san.

16:03.850 --> 16:06.550
I'll steal you away from Akihiko.

16:07.060 --> 16:07.870
What?

16:08.720 --> 16:09.870
I love you.

16:12.650 --> 16:14.830
Ex-Excuse me!

16:20.700 --> 16:23.200
<i>What was that? What did he just say!?</i>

16:23.430 --> 16:24.390
<i>Steal me!?</i>

16:24.820 --> 16:27.750
<i>Elder Usagi loves me!? Why!?</i>

16:27.990 --> 16:34.150
<i>And besides, besides! I am most clearly and certainly a boy!!</i>

16:37.860 --> 16:39.440
<i>The younger Usami!!!</i>

16:39.500 --> 16:40.630
What are you talking about?

16:42.560 --> 16:43.660
Nothing, nothing!

16:43.820 --> 16:47.390
There was this mountain of strawberries, and the conversation just didn't mesh...

16:47.490 --> 16:52.490
And yet all of a sudden... I... but I definitely... I...

16:51.500 --> 16:56.930
tremble

16:52.490 --> 16:54.720
...Am I releasing some kind of weird pheromones!?

16:54.720 --> 16:56.760
Is your head alright?

16:57.530 --> 16:59.440
What happened? Calm down.

16:59.530 --> 17:01.830
You disappeared suddenly, so I was worried.

17:04.920 --> 17:05.930
What happened?

17:07.060 --> 17:09.260
Sorry. It's nothing.

17:09.770 --> 17:13.390
Would a person saying nothing happened just flat out rush into the room like this?

17:16.270 --> 17:19.250
Um, I was going to the bathroom,

17:19.580 --> 17:21.860
and ran into your brother by chance.

17:23.040 --> 17:24.520
He was staying here?

17:25.360 --> 17:30.910
Yeah. So then, we started talking a bit because of was happened yesterday...

17:31.300 --> 17:39.250
Then all of a sudden, he started saying weird stuff like he'll steal me away from Usagi-san and such...

17:41.350 --> 17:44.460
W-Wait Usagi-san!

17:44.510 --> 17:46.620
I might have just heard wrong!

17:46.720 --> 17:49.830
No attacking! No violence!

17:50.230 --> 17:53.950
Snatching away other people's things is exactly the kind of thing he would do!

17:53.990 --> 17:55.570
What do you mean by "things"!?

17:55.700 --> 17:57.500
Don't treat me like a thing!

17:57.660 --> 18:01.110
I've never treated you like a thing, but you belong to me.

18:01.290 --> 18:02.460
Who decided that!?

18:02.560 --> 18:03.610
I decided that!

18:04.310 --> 18:05.910
What's with that!?

18:07.310 --> 18:09.290
Akihiko, get out here!

18:09.380 --> 18:11.600
It's the afterparty, show your damn face at least!

18:11.660 --> 18:13.820
I did everything I had to!

18:14.310 --> 18:16.710
You all can take care of the rest!

18:16.970 --> 18:18.120
Don't kid me!

18:18.240 --> 18:20.980
Throw in some hours as a service!

18:21.450 --> 18:23.430
What do you think work really means!?

18:23.790 --> 18:26.030
That kind of thing is your job, right?

18:26.800 --> 18:28.090
Akihiko, damn you...!

18:29.410 --> 18:30.450
Do as you like!

18:32.000 --> 18:34.250
Usagi-san, you should go!

18:34.670 --> 18:36.710
It'd be real bad if it affects your work.

18:37.020 --> 18:38.000
No need.

18:38.410 --> 18:39.550
My work's done.

18:39.830 --> 18:41.140
It's now my private time.

18:42.430 --> 18:45.520
And my number one personal priority is you!

18:48.740 --> 18:55.010
Listen, no matter what anyone says, I'll say it as many times as it takes, so that you don't forget.

18:56.480 --> 18:57.430
Remember,

18:58.130 --> 19:00.140
You belong to me, forever.

19:00.800 --> 19:01.740
Just give in.

19:04.680 --> 19:07.490
No, no, no, no! I won't give in!

19:07.790 --> 19:09.390
I won't give in!

19:09.760 --> 19:12.400
Till when can that stubbornness last, I wonder.

19:12.600 --> 19:14.930
Forever, till eternity!

19:15.370 --> 19:17.760
Then, it's upto me to make you understand.

19:22.530 --> 19:24.980
W-Wai... Usagi-san!

19:35.150 --> 19:36.900
No... not here...

19:37.600 --> 19:38.950
Nobody is watching.

19:39.730 --> 19:41.390
That's not the problem...

19:42.320 --> 19:45.320
Misaki... I thought I told you to just give in.

19:50.550 --> 19:51.460
Misaki.

19:52.530 --> 19:54.490
The window looks like a mirror.

19:56.000 --> 19:58.840
Pervert! Idiot Usagi! Shitty Usagi!

19:59.410 --> 20:01.400
I absolutely hate you!

20:03.110 --> 20:04.260
I love you.

20:08.110 --> 20:09.120
<i>Annoying...</i>

20:09.940 --> 20:15.030
<i>Like a knife, he violates me even through my ears...</i>

20:17.180 --> 20:20.810
Tomorrow, should we check out of the hotel early?

20:21.550 --> 20:24.710
Huh, okay. But why?

20:25.370 --> 20:27.790
It'll be a pain if we run into Isaka-san.

20:29.160 --> 20:31.650
Cause trouble for others

20:33.050 --> 20:35.540
<i>What should I do...?</i>

20:36.590 --> 20:39.040
<i>Causing trouble for Usagi-san is something I...</i>

20:40.520 --> 20:43.670
<i>But, I don't want to think of anything right now.</i>

20:45.150 --> 20:47.550
What's wrong? Feeling sleepy?

20:49.070 --> 20:50.300
Then sleep.

20:51.170 --> 20:52.130
Yeah.

20:53.750 --> 20:56.110
<i>All I want to feel now is...</i>

20:57.410 --> 21:00.470
<i>...Usagi-san's big hands, his warmth,</i>

21:01.270 --> 21:02.450
<i>the smell of his cigarettes,</i>

21:03.810 --> 21:04.960
<i>his gentle voice...</i>

21:08.130 --> 21:11.400
Room service for Takahashi Misaki-sama!

21:12.970 --> 21:15.810
Are you sure these were not for Usami Akihiko?

21:16.100 --> 21:18.950
No, these were definitely for Takahashi-sama.

21:19.910 --> 21:23.710
The sender is Usami Haruhiko-sama.

21:25.430 --> 21:26.610
Strawberries?

21:29.510 --> 21:32.790
<i>Nii-chan, I can't look Usagi-san in the face.</i>

21:44.850 --> 21:49.990
Yokogiru dake wa ichinichi no owari ni

21:44.850 --> 21:49.990
Crossing paths at the end of the day,

21:50.120 --> 21:55.380
itsu kara ka kimi ga sakimawari shite matte ite

21:50.120 --> 21:55.380
at some point you went up ahead and waited for me.

21:55.730 --> 22:00.750
ureshii kimochi bai ni shite kurete

21:55.730 --> 22:00.750
You doubled all my happiness,

22:00.750 --> 22:07.440
kanamishi kimochi hanbun ni shite kureru kara

22:00.750 --> 22:07.440
and halved all my sadness.

22:07.550 --> 22:12.550
kore kara donna michi aruitemo

22:07.550 --> 22:12.550
No matter what path I walk in the future,

22:12.950 --> 22:17.230
kitto sore wa kimi he to tsuzuiteru

22:12.950 --> 22:17.230
will surely lead to you.

22:17.230 --> 22:19.990
boku no saki ni wa kimi ga ite

22:17.230 --> 22:19.990
You're there up ahead of me,

22:19.990 --> 22:22.850
kimi no saki ni wa boka ga iru

22:19.990 --> 22:22.850
I'm there ahead of you,

22:22.850 --> 22:28.120
hoka no dare mo inai futari dake no basho

22:22.850 --> 22:28.120
A place for just the two of us with no one else around.

22:28.120 --> 22:34.020
sore ga boku no subete nanda sore ga boku wo karuku shiteru na

22:28.120 --> 22:34.020
That's my everything, and lifts the weight off my shoulders.

22:34.610 --> 22:39.090
mou doko he mo ikanaide

22:34.610 --> 22:39.090
Hey, don't go anywhere.

22:39.090 --> 22:44.550
yakusoku no basho wa itsumo hidamari no kaori wo sasete

22:39.090 --> 22:44.550
Our promised place always has the smell of sunshine.

22:44.550 --> 22:49.940
boku no ashimoto wo terashiteirunda

22:44.550 --> 22:49.940
It's casting a light at my feet.

22:49.940 --> 22:55.760
kimi no koto ga suki da yotte to ieru boku ga suki dakara

22:49.940 --> 22:55.760
I love myself being able to say "I love you!"

22:56.150 --> 23:01.440
mune no oku de sotto arigatou

22:56.150 --> 23:01.440
Softly in my heart I say, "Thank you."

23:05.260 --> 23:08.600
Takahashi-kun's Strawberry Life!

23:08.700 --> 23:11.680
Note: Text are the different types of strawberries.

23:12.300 --> 23:15.400
Freshly picked morning strawberries really are the best!

23:15.790 --> 23:17.950
I love~ strawberries!

23:17.950 --> 23:21.440
From left to right: Mille-feullie, strawberry milk, chocolate, strawberry daifuku, pudding, tart, shortcake, parfait

23:21.640 --> 23:23.840
Strawberry sweets are like a fairy tale!

23:23.880 --> 23:26.190
I love~ strawberries!

23:29.360 --> 23:34.720
<i>Nii-chan, I never dreamt that the day would come when I would be tormented by strawberries.</i>

23:36.510 --> 23:40.800
Ah, Ah, test, test, the sun will come out today, we're back, this is a mike test,

23:40.800 --> 23:44.470
the sun will come out today, we're back, this is a mike test, Ah, Ah.

23:44.470 --> 23:46.470
